>
>here are some monsters I consider dangerous, in order of the character
>level they are most likely to cause the downfall of:
>
>floating eye, nymph, gnome with wand of sleep, black pudding, air elemental,
>Olog-Hai, minotaur, black dragon, master lich, Archon, Angel.

If you say dangerous='kills you more often than anything else', 
someone wrote a (perl?) script which would look through your score list
and prints out the worst monsters (based on how often they kill you, and
how strong the character was when they killed it).  I never got the 
script to work though (I guess perl isn't all that portable), so I can't
tell you who the most dangerous is for me.

If you say dangerous='powerful' (the thing I'd least like to meet in a 
dark alley) I'd say Archon or Master Lich from the above list are by
far the worst.  Sure, any monster with a wand or a ray attack is 
dangerous until you get reflection, but even when you are well equiped, 
those monsters could worry you a little.  Master Liches because they can 
summon other monsters and destroy your armor, Archons because they often 
have reflection and a named weapon.
